(Chile 2001)_01,C_EXPRESS_OBSCENE,False,,True,1.0,"Article 24 d) The procedure shall be subject to the following rules: d) The final judgment shall be issued within the third day after the expiration of the period referred to in the previous letter, whether or not the defendant has submitted pleadings. If the court ordered an evidentiary hearing, this term shall run once the term set for it has expired.

Article 29.- Personal appreciations formulated in specialized commentary of political, literary, historical, artistic, scientific, technical and sports criticism shall not constitute injuries, unless their tenor reveals the purpose of injuring in addition to criticizing.

Article 30.- Facts relating to a person's sexual, conjugal, family or domestic life shall be considered pertinent to the private sphere of persons, unless they constitute a crime."
