(Chile 2001)_01,C_EXPRESS_PROPERTY,False,,True,1.0,"Article 9.- In cases where the law allows the owner of a media outlet to be a natural person, that person shall have domicile in the country and shall not have been convicted of a crime that merits an afflictive penalty. In the case of legal persons, they shall have domicile in Chile and be incorporated in the country or have an authorized agency to operate in national territory. Their president and their administrators or legal representatives shall be Chilean and shall not have been convicted of a crime that merits an afflictive penalty."
