(Chile 2001)_01,C_EXPRESS_RELIGION,True,1.0,True,1.0,"Article 8.- A journalist or person engaged in journalistic activity shall not be compelled to act in contravention of the ethical norms generally accepted for the exercise of their profession.

Article 11.- The preceding provisions shall not apply to publications that are distributed internally in public or private institutions.

Article 19.- The written clarification or rectification shall be published in full, without intercalations, on the same page, with characteristics similar to the information that provoked it or, failing that, in a prominent place in the same section.

Article 19.- In the case of free-to-air sound broadcasting or television services or limited television services, the clarification or rectification shall be broadcast in the same schedule and with characteristics similar to the transmission that motivated it.

Article 30 f) For the purposes of this Article, the following shall be considered facts of public interest of a person: f) Those consisting of the commission of crimes or culpable participation in them.

Article 39.- The director or the person who legally replaces them shall also be considered an author, in the case of media outlets, at the time of publication or dissemination, unless it is proven that there was no negligence on their part.

Article 41.- This rule of competence shall prevail over any other that could alter its effects, due to the connection of the crimes, the concurrence of offenders or the immunity enjoyed by any of the accused."
