(Chile 2001)_01,C_EXPRESS_REPUTATION,True,1.0,True,1.0,"Article 7.- Anyone who makes use of the right enshrined in the first paragraph shall be personally responsible for the crimes that they may commit by the information disseminated.

Article 16.- Any natural or legal person offended or unjustly alluded to by any media outlet shall have the right to have their clarification or rectification freely disseminated, under the conditions established in the following articles, by the media outlet in which such information was issued.

Article 18.- The obligation of the media outlet to disseminate the clarification or rectification free of charge shall apply even when the information that motivates it comes from an insertion. In this case, the media outlet may charge the cost incurred for the clarification or rectification to the person who ordered the insertion.

Article 18.- Clarifications and rectifications shall in any case be limited to the object of the information that motivates them and may not exceed one thousand words or, in the case of free-to-air sound broadcasting or television services or limited television services, two minutes.

Article 21.- The right of clarification or rectification may not be exercised with respect to personal appreciations that are formulated in specialized commentary of political, literary, historical, artistic, scientific, technical and sports criticism, without prejudice to the sanction that these articles may give rise to if, by means of their dissemination, some of the crimes punished in this law are committed.

Article 22.- Once the judgment is final, the court shall apply a new fine for each publication appearing or transmission carried out without compliance with the respective obligation. In the case of infringement of Articles 9, first paragraph, 10 and 11, the court shall also order the suspension of the media outlet while the non-compliance subsists.

Article 28.- The court, in the resolution that orders the publication or broadcast of the clarification or rectification, or its correction, shall set a period for it and, furthermore, may apply to the director a fine of four to twelve monthly tax units.

Article 28.- Once the conviction judgment is final, if the clarification or rectification is not published within the period indicated by the court, and in the terms established in the first and second paragraphs of Article 19, as the case may be, the director of the medium shall be sanctioned with a fine of twelve to one hundred monthly tax units and the immediate suspension of the media outlet shall be ordered. The court shall lift the suspension ordered from the moment the director pays the fine and attaches a sworn statement in which they undertake to fully comply with the obligation imposed in the first next edition or transmission.

Article 29.- The crimes of calumny and injury committed through any media outlet shall be punished with the corporal penalties indicated in Articles 413, 418, first paragraph, and 419 of the Penal Code, and with fines of twenty to one hundred and fifty monthly tax units in the cases of number 1 of Article 413 and Article 418; twenty to one hundred monthly tax units in the case of number 2 of Article 413; and twenty to fifty monthly tax units in the case of Article 419.

Article 31.- Anyone who, by any media outlet, publishes or transmits material intended to promote hatred or hostility against persons or collectives on the grounds of their race, sex, religion or nationality shall be punished with a fine of twenty-five to one hundred monthly tax units. In case of repetition, the fine may be increased to two hundred monthly tax units.

Article 32.- The dissemination of news or information emanating from pending or related trials, proceedings or judicial steps may not be invoked as exculpatory or mitigating of civil or criminal liability when such dissemination, by itself, constitutes the crimes of calumny, injury or public outrage to good morals.

Article 33.- A violation of this Article shall be sanctioned with a fine of thirty to one hundred and fifty monthly tax units. In the case of repetition, the fine shall be doubled.

Article 34.- Anyone who commits one of the crimes of public outrage to good morals contemplated in Articles 373 and 374 of the Penal Code, through a media outlet, shall be punished with minor imprisonment in its minimum to medium degree and a fine of eleven to eighty monthly tax units.

Article 34.- An aggravating circumstance of public outrage to good morals shall be the incitement or promotion of the perversion of minors or that the crime is committed within a radius of two hundred meters of a school, college, institute or any educational or asylum establishment intended for children and young people.

Article 35.- Media outlets shall be exempt from criminal liability regarding the publication of the opinions expressed by parliamentarians in the cases indicated in the first paragraph of Article 58 of the Political Constitution, and from the pleadings made by lawyers before the courts of justice.

Article 36.- Whoever, outside the cases provided for by the Constitution or the law, and in the exercise of public functions, obstructs or prevents the free dissemination of opinions or information through any media outlet, shall suffer the penalty of minor imprisonment in its minimum degree or a fine of forty to one hundred monthly tax units.

Article 40.- The civil action to obtain compensation for damages and losses arising from crimes punished in this law shall be governed by the general rules.

Article 41.- Ordinary justice shall always be competent to hear the crimes committed by civilians by reason or on account of the exercise of the freedoms of opinion and information declared in the first paragraph of number 12 of Article 19 of the Political Constitution of the Republic.

Article 45.- The following final paragraph is incorporated into Article 504 of the Code of Criminal Procedure: ""The conviction under Article 374 of the Penal Code shall order the total or partial destruction, as appropriate, of the printed matters or sound or audiovisual recordings of any kind that were seized during the proceedings.""

Article 46 b) In Law No. 12,927 on State Security, Article 16 is repealed.

Article 46 c) In Law No. 12,927 on State Security, Article 17 is replaced by the following: ""Article 17.- Criminal liability for the crimes provided for and punished in this law, committed through a media outlet, shall be determined in accordance with the provisions of Article 39 of the law on the freedoms of opinion and information and the practice of journalism."".

Article 46 d) In Law No. 12,927 on State Security, Articles 18, 19, 20 and 21 are repealed."
