(Chile 2001)_01,GOV_OVERSIGHT,False,,True,1.0,"Article 9.- The sentence imposing the penalty indicated shall immediately terminate the affected person in all functions or activities related to the direction, administration or representation in the media outlet in which they perform them.

Article 9.- Every media outlet shall provide reliable information regarding its owners, direct or indirect controllers, lessees, users, borrowers or concessionaires, as applicable. If they are one or more persons, such information shall include what is conducive to identifying the natural and legal persons who participate in ownership or have its use under any title. It shall also include copies of the documents proving the constitution and bylaws of legal persons that are partners or shareholders, except in the case of open joint-stock companies, as well as their amendments, as appropriate. Such information shall be freely accessible to the public and shall be permanently updated and available at the domicile of the respective media outlet and to the authorities that require it in the exercise of their competencies.

Article 11 e) The commencement of activities of written media outlets shall be reported to the Provincial Governor's Office or Regional Intendancy corresponding to the domicile of the medium by means of a declaration, of which that Governor's Office or Intendancy shall send a copy to the Director of the National Library. The declaration shall contain the following statements: e) In the case of a legal person, the documents in which its partners or shareholders and the percentage, amount and modalities of their participation in ownership or in the company's capital are recorded or, where appropriate, the documents of the opening of the agency, its bylaws and the mandates of its legal representatives.

Article 11.- Any change that occurs in the aforementioned mentions shall also be communicated in the same manner within the following fifteen days, or within sixty days if it affects any of those referred to in letter e). However, changes in shareholders or in the participation in the capital shall not need to be reported when the owner of the media outlet is an open joint-stock company.

Article 11.- The Director of the National Library shall keep an updated register of the written media outlets existing in the country, indicating the data referred to in this Article.

Article 22.- The director and the owner or concessionaire of the media outlet shall be jointly and severally liable for the payment of the fines.

Article 28.- The director and the owner or concessionaire of the media outlet shall be jointly and severally liable for the payment of the fines."
