(Chile 2001)_01,IM_PREVENTION,False,,True,1.0,"Article 14.- The persons or establishments referred to in the previous article shall send to the National Library, at the time of their publication, five copies of every printed material, regardless of its nature.

Article 19.- The director of the media outlet may not refuse to disseminate the clarification or rectification, except that it does not comply with the requirements of the second paragraph of Article 18, or implies the commission of a crime. Its refusal shall be presumed if the clarification or rectification is not disseminated at the time indicated in the foregoing paragraph, or if it is not published or broadcast under the terms established in the first or second paragraphs, as appropriate.

Article 23.- These infractions may be denounced by any person and, in particular, by the Provincial Governor or the Regional Intendant or the Director of the National Library, in the case of Article 11."
