(Venezuela 2000)_02,C_EXPRESS_OBSCENE,False,,True,1.0,ARTICLE 159.- The sanctions that may be imposed for the infractions and crimes typified in this Law are: 1. Public admonition; 2. Fine; 3. Revocation of the administrative authorization or concession; 4. Cessation of clandestine activities; 5. Disqualification; 6. Confiscation of equipment and materials used for the activity; 7. Imprisonment.
