(Venezuela 2000)_02,C_EXPRESS_ORDER,False,,True,1.0,"ARTICLE 166.- A fine of up to fifty thousand Tax Units (50,000 T.U.), in accordance with what the Regulation of this Law provides, shall be imposed for: 4. Failure to comply with requests from the National Telecommunications Commission, within the time and conditions it determines, relating to the cessation of radioelectric emissions that produce harmful interference.

ARTICLE 170.- In case of recidivism in the violations or non-compliances provided for in this Chapter, the National Telecommunications Commission shall impose fines successively increased by twenty-five percent (25%) up to the maximum limit provided for the type, without prejudice to the revocation of the corresponding administrative authorization or concession.

ARTICLE 171.- Without prejudice to the fines that correspond to be applied in accordance with the provisions of this Law, the revocation of the administrative authorization or concession, as the case may be, shall be imposed on: 6. The person who uses or permits the use of the telecommunications services for which he is authorized, as means to aid in the commission of crimes.

ARTICLE 171.- Without prejudice to the fines that correspond to be applied in accordance with the provisions of this Law, the revocation of the administrative authorization or concession, as the case may be, shall be imposed on: 7. The person who knowingly supplies information to the National Telecommunications Commission based on documents declared false by a final sentence.

ARTICLE 173.- Without prejudice to the fines that correspond to be applied in accordance with the provisions of this Law, confiscation of equipment and materials used in the installation, operation, provision or exploitation of said services or activities shall be imposed on whoever: 1. Makes clandestine use of the radioelectric spectrum; 2. Reoffends in the installation, operation, provision or exploitation of networks or telecommunications services without holding the respective authorization; 3. Does not comply with the decision of the National Telecommunications Commission derived from the revocation of an administrative authorization or concession, as the case may be.

ARTICLE 188.- Shall be punished with imprisonment of four to twelve months: 1. Whoever through gross negligence causes damage to terminal equipment intended for public access, installations or telecommunications systems, so as to interrupt partially or prevent the provision of the service; 2. Whoever through gross negligence causes harmful interference that interrupts partially or prevents the provision of the service; 3. Whoever uses or enjoys fraudulently a telecommunications service or facility.

ARTICLE 189.- Shall be punished with imprisonment of one to four years: 1. Whoever with intent causes damage to terminal equipment, installations or telecommunications systems, in such a way that the provision of the service is partially or totally interrupted; 2. Whoever, using equipment or technologies of any type, provides to a third party access to or enjoyment in a fraudulent or improper manner of a telecommunications service or facility; 3. Whoever clandestinely uses the radioelectric spectrum. It shall be understood that there is clandestine use of the radioelectric spectrum when, in cases where a concession is required, there is not at least the corresponding frequency reservation; 4. Whoever produces harmful interference with the specific purpose of generating the interruption of a telecommunications service.

ARTICLE 191.- No natural or legal person or group of persons may, by themselves or through an intermediary, obtain by concession or come to control more than one broadcasting or open television station in the same frequency band per locality. The same restriction applies in relation to the shareholders of a concessionary company."
