(Venezuela 2000)_02,C_EXPRESS_REPUTATION,False,,True,1.0,"ARTICLE 165.- A fine of up to thirty thousand Tax Units (30,000 T.U.), in accordance with what the Regulation of this Law provides, shall be imposed for: 6. The emission or transmission of false or misleading identification signals by an operator, which may induce error in users or in the National Telecommunications Commission regarding the authorship of such emissions or transmissions.

ARTICLE 168.- For the purpose of the determination by the National Telecommunications Commission of the amount of the fines referred to in this Law, the following aggravating situations shall be considered: 1. Their continuing nature; 2. The effect on the service; 3. The obtaining of economic benefits by the offender; 4. Clandestinity; 5. The lack of homologation or certification of the devices or equipment used.

ARTICLE 169.- For the purpose of the imposition of the fines referred to in this Law, the following mitigating situations shall be considered: 1. Having acknowledged in the course of the procedure the existence of the infringement; 2. Having remedied on one's own initiative the infringement situation and fully repaired the damages that may have been caused.

ARTICLE 190.- Illegal interception, interference, copying or disclosure of the content of transmissions and communications shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the special Law on the matter."
(Venezuela 2000)_02,I_EXPRESS_REPUTATION,False,,False,,
(Venezuela 2000)_02,P_EXPRESS_REPUTATION,False,,True,1.0,"ARTICLE 23.- Administrative authorization shall not be required for the installation or operation of telecommunications equipment or networks, in the following cases: 1. When they are security or intercommunication equipment that, without connection to public networks and without using the public radioelectric domain, are used inside a property or to serve certain properties;

ARTICLE 197.- Telecommunications operators may lease circuits or resell capacity in their systems, provided that they do so in transparent terms and on non-discriminatory conditions and not harmful to free competition. In no case may the operations referred to in this article be carried out to the detriment of the quality of services or the rights of users."
