(Venezuela 2000)_01,C_EXPRESS_NATSEC,True,1.0,True,1.0,"Article 186.- If by divulging the content the guilty party has caused some prejudice, the penalty shall be fifteen days to ten months of arrest.

Article 211.- If the act provided in the preceding paragraph has been committed publicly, the arrest may be imposed for up to two years.

Article 224.- If the act provided in the preceding article has been accompanied by violence or threat, it shall be punished with imprisonment of three to eighteen months.

Article 226.- If the guilty party has made use of violence or threats, the imprisonment shall be six months to three years."
