(Venezuela 2000)_01,C_EXPRESS_OBSCENE,False,,True,1.0,"Article 134.- The penalty shall be increased by one third if the guilty party had the drawings, plans or documents, or had acquired the knowledge of the secrets by reason of his employment, public office or functions. The penalty shall likewise be increased in the same manner if by fraud, theft or violence the acquisition of such knowledge or of those objects has been made.

Article 150.- The penalty shall be increased proportionally by one half if the offense has been committed while the aforementioned Corporations are exercising their official functions.

Article 187.- If the act has caused some prejudice, the arrest may not be less than forty-five days.

Article 189.- If any of the acts provided in this article causes some prejudice, the imprisonment penalty shall be three months to two years.

Article 225.- When any of the acts provided in the preceding articles has been committed against a public official not because of his functions but at the very moment of exercising them, the same penalties shall be applied reduced by one third to one half.

Article 244.- (2) The individual who, having manifested before the authority his name and circumstances, should not have been considered as a witness or was not warned of the faculty he had of abstaining from declaring.

Article 249.- When the false testimony, expert report or interpretation have been retracted in the manner and at the time indicated in Article 245, the penalty incurred by the guilty party of the offense provided in Article 247 shall be diminished in the proportion of one sixth to one third.

Article 448.- When, in the cases provided in the two preceding articles, a person has been driven to the crime by violences executed against his person, he shall not be punishable.

Article 449.- The offenses contained in the writings submitted by the parties or their representatives, or in the speeches pronounced by them at the bar before the Judge, during the course of a trial, shall not give rise to action; but independently of the application of the disciplinary provisions of the case, which the Tribunal shall impose, that authority may order the total or partial suppression of the defamatory matter, and if the aggrieved party requests it, may also prudently accord pecuniary reparation when pronouncing on the cause.

Article 450.- In case of conviction for any of the crimes specified in the present Chapter, the Judge shall order the confiscation and suppression of the printed materials, drawings and other objects that have served to commit the crime; and if it is writings in respect of which suppression cannot be ordered, he shall order that a reference to the sentence pronounced in relation to the case be made in their margin.

Article 451.- If the aggrieved party dies before making use of his action, or if the crimes have been committed against the memory of a deceased person, the accusation or complaint may be promoted by the spouse, the ascendants, the descendants, the brothers or sisters, nephews, the in-laws in direct line and by the immediate heirs.

Article 495.- Whoever, selling or distributing printed materials, drawings or manuscripts in a public place or open to the public, shall have advertised them with cries or with news capable of causing disturbance to public tranquility or to individuals, shall be punished with a fine of one hundred bolívares."
