(Venezuela 2000)_01,C_EXPRESS_REPUTATION,True,1.0,True,1.0,"Article 158.- If the punishable act is one that does not permit ex officio procedure, trial shall not proceed except at the instance of the foreign Government.

Article 239.- Any individual who, called by the judicial authority in the capacity of witness, expert, doctor, surgeon or interpreter, excuses himself from appearing without justified motive shall be punished with imprisonment of fifteen days to three months. Whoever, having appeared, refuses without legal reason his depositions or the performance of the office that motivated his summoning shall incur the same penalty. In addition to imprisonment, the guilty party shall be disqualified from exercising his profession or art for a time equal to the imprisonment once it has concluded.

Article 240.- Whoever reports to the judicial authority or to some investigating official a supposed or imaginary punishable fact shall be punished with imprisonment of one to fifteen months. Whoever simulates the traces of a punishable fact, so that it gives rise to a principle of investigation, shall be imposed the same penalty. Whoever before this judicial authority falsely declares that he has committed or helped to commit some punishable fact, so that it gives rise to a principle of investigation, unless his declaration is with the object of saving some close relative, a close friend or his benefactor, shall likewise incur the same penalty.

Article 241.- The guilty party shall be punished with imprisonment for a time of eighteen months to five years in the following cases: (1) When the imputed crime merits corporal punishment that exceeds thirty months; (2) When the false accusation has caused the conviction to a corporal penalty of lesser duration.

Article 241.- If the imposed conviction has been to a presidio penalty, the calumniator shall be imposed the penalty of five years of imprisonment.

Article 245.- If the retraction takes place after or if it refers to a false deposition in civil trial, the penalty shall be diminished by one third to one half, provided that the retraction takes place before the definitive decision of the matter.

Article 246.- The provisions of the preceding articles shall also be applicable to experts and interpreters who, called in the capacity of such before the judicial authority, give false reports, information or interpretations; who shall also be punished with disqualification for the exercise of their profession or art for a time equal to the imprisonment, once it has concluded.

Article 247.- Whoever has bribed a witness, expert or interpreter with the object of causing him to commit the offense provided in Article 243 shall be punished, when the false testimony, expert report or interpretation have been effected, with the following penalties: (1) In the case of the first part of the cited article, with imprisonment of forty-five days to eighteen months.

Article 247.- Whoever by means of threats, gifts or offerings has only attempted to bribe a witness, expert or interpreter shall incur in the penalties established in the preceding provisions but limited to one third.

Article 248.- If the guilty party of the offense provided in the preceding article is the accused himself or his close relatives or whenever he has not exposed another person to criminal proceedings or to a conviction, the established penalties shall be reduced by one half to two thirds.

Article 250.- Whoever, being a party in a civil trial, incurs perjury shall be punished with imprisonment of three to fifteen months. If the guilty party retracts before finishing the litigation, the imprisonment shall be fifteen days to three months.

Article 284.- Whoever publicly instigates another to commit a determined infraction shall be punished, by the sole fact of the instigation: (1) If it is a crime for which a presidio penalty has been established, with imprisonment of ten to thirty months.

Article 493.- Any individual who, without complying with the prescriptions of the law, shall exercise the typographic art, lithography or any other art that consists of reproducing multiple copies by chemical or mechanical processes, shall be punished with a fine of one hundred to seven hundred bolívares.

Article 496.- Whoever shall have affixed by himself or through others printed materials, drawings or manuscripts, without permission of the authority if such permission is required by law, or outside the points or places in which fixation is permitted, shall be punished with a fine of ten to fifty bolívares."
