(Algeria 2006)_01,C_EXPRESS_OBSCENE,True,1.0,True,1.0,"Art. 11. Except in cases where the law provides otherwise, and without prejudice to the rights of the defense, the procedure during the inquiry and the instruction is secret. Any person who takes part in this procedure is bound to professional secrecy under the conditions and under the penalties provided in the Penal Code. However, in order to avoid the spread of partial or inaccurate information, or to put an end to a disturbance of public order, only the representative of the public prosecution may make public objective elements drawn from the procedure that contain no assessment on the merits of the charges brought against the persons under investigation.

Art. 65 bis 12. Infiltration consists, for an officer or an agent of the judicial police acting under the responsibility of an officer of the judicial police charged with coordinating the operation, in monitoring persons suspected of committing a crime or an offense by passing, before these persons, as one of their co-authors, accomplices or receivers. The officer or the agent of the judicial police is, for this purpose, authorized to use a borrowed identity and, if necessary, to commit the acts mentioned in Article 65 bis 14 below. Under penalty of nullity, these acts may not constitute an inducement to commit offences.

Art. 417 bis 1. Is punished by the penalty of criminal imprisonment for life: anyone who knowingly communicates a false information which he knows to be of a nature to compromise the safety of an aircraft in flight or of a ship."
