(Algeria 2006)_01,C_EXPRESS_REPUTATION,True,1.0,True,1.0,"Art. 69 bis. Whoever reveals the identity of these officers or agents of the judicial police is punished with imprisonment of two (2) years to five (5) years and a fine of 50,000 DA to 200,000 DA. If the revelation has caused violence, blows and wounds against one of these persons or against their spouses, children and direct ascendants, it is punished with imprisonment of five (5) years to ten (10) years and a fine of 200,000 DA to 500,000 DA. If the revelation has caused the death of one of these persons, it is punished with imprisonment of ten (10) years to twenty (20) years and a fine of 500,000 DA to 1,000,000 DA, without prejudice, where applicable, to the application of the provisions of Chapter I of Title II of Book III of the Penal Code.

Art. 18. In cases determined by law, the court of judgment may order that its decision of condemnation be published in full or by extracts in one or more newspapers that it designates or be posted in the places that it indicates, all at the expense of the convicted, provided that the publication costs may not exceed the sum fixed for that purpose by the decision of condemnation, nor that the duration of posting exceed one month. The fact of removing, hiding or tearing totally or partially the posters affixed pursuant to the preceding paragraph is punished with imprisonment of three (3) months to two (2) years and a fine of 25,000 DA to 200,000 DA. The judgment will order anew the execution of the posting at the expense of the author.

Art. 298. Any defamation committed against private individuals is punished with imprisonment of two (2) to six (6) months and a fine of 25,000 DA to 50,000 DA or with one of these two penalties only. The pardon of the victim puts an end to criminal proceedings.

Art. 299. Any insult committed against one or several persons is punished with imprisonment of one (1) to three (3) months and a fine of 10,000 DA to 25,000 DA. The pardon of the victim puts an end to criminal proceedings.

Art. 303. Whoever, in bad faith and outside the cases provided by Article 137, opens or removes letters or correspondence addressed to third parties, is punished with imprisonment of one (1) month to one (1) year and a fine of 25,000 DA to 100,000 DA or with one of these two penalties only.

Art. 303 bis. Whoever, by any process, voluntarily infringes the privacy of others is punished with imprisonment of six (6) months to three (3) years and a fine of 50,000 DA to 300,000 DA: 1 - by capturing, recording or transmitting without authorization or consent their communications, words pronounced privately or confidentially; 2 - by taking, recording or transmitting without authorization or consent the image of a person present in a private place. The attempt of the offence provided by this article is punished with the same penalties as the consummated offence. The pardon of the victim puts an end to criminal proceedings.

Art. 303 bis 1. Whoever preserves, carries or allows to be known to the public or to a third party, or uses in any way, any recording, image or document obtained by means of one of the acts provided by Article 303 bis, is punished with the penalties provided in the previous article. If the offence provided in the preceding paragraph is committed by the press, the special provisions provided by the laws relating thereto to determine the persons responsible are applicable.

Art. 303 bis 2. In the event of a conviction for the offenses referred to in articles 303 bis and 303 bis 1, the court may pronounce the deprivation of one or several of the rights provided for in article 9 bis1 for a duration not exceeding five (5) years; it may also order the publication of the judgment of conviction according to the procedures provided for in article 18 of this law. The confiscation of objects having been used for the commission of the offense is always pronounced."
