(Algeria 2006)_01,GOV_REGULATOR,False,,True,1.0,"Art. 65 bis 10. The judicial police officer authorized or appointed describes or transcribes in a report, which is filed in the case file, the correspondences, the images or the conversations recorded, which are useful for the manifestation of the truth. Conversations in a foreign language are transcribed and translated, where appropriate, with the assistance of an interpreter required for this purpose. The judge who authorized the operation may at any time order its interruption before the expiry of the fixed duration. The authorization is filed in the case file after completion of the infiltration operation.

Art. 65 bis 11. When the necessities of the inquiry or the instruction relating to one of the offences enumerated in Article 65 bis 5 justify it, the public prosecutor or, after the advice of this magistrate, the investigating judge may authorize that, under their control, an infiltration operation be carried out under the conditions provided in the following articles. If a judicial information has been opened, this authorization is given by the investigating judge. The operations thus authorized take place under his direct control.

Art. 65 bis 13. Infiltration is the subject of a report drafted by the judicial police officer who coordinated the operation, which includes only the elements strictly necessary for the establishment of the offences and which does not endanger the security of the infiltrated officer or agent as well as the persons required in accordance with Article 65 bis 14.

Art. 65 bis 17. In the event of a decision to interrupt the operation or at the expiry of the period fixed by the decision authorizing the infiltration and in the absence of a prolongation, the infiltrated agent may continue the activities mentioned in Article 65 bis 14, without being criminally responsible, for the strictly necessary time to enable him to cease his surveillance under conditions ensuring his security, provided that such duration may not exceed four (4) months. The magistrate having issued the authorization referred to in Article 65 bis 11 is informed as soon as possible. If, at the end of the four-month period, the infiltrated agent cannot cease his operation in conditions ensuring his security, that magistrate authorizes the prolongation for a duration not exceeding four (4) months."
(Algeria 2006)_01,GOV_REGULATOR_CRISIS,False,,False,,
(Algeria 2006)_01,GOV_WARRANT,False,,True,1.0,"Art. 47 bis. When, during a flagrante delicto investigation or an investigation relating to one of the offenses referred to in Article 47 paragraph 3 of this law, the person at whose dwelling a search is made is placed in police custody or detained elsewhere and transporting that person to the place appears likely to be avoided for reasons of serious risk either of a disturbance of public order or of escape, or of disappearance of evidence during the time necessary for transport, the search may be carried out with the prior agreement of the public prosecutor or the investigating judge, in the presence of two witnesses required in accordance with the provisions of Article 45 of this law or in the presence of a representative designated by the person whose dwelling is to be searched. When the search is carried out in premises occupied by a person bound by the law to professional secrecy, the judicial police officer has the obligation to take beforehand all useful measures so that the respect for that professional secrecy is guaranteed. The seized objects and documents are closed and sealed, if possible with written characters; if they cannot receive written characters, they are placed in a container or bag on which the judicial police officer attaches a strip of paper which he seals with his seal. An inventory of the objects and documents seized is drawn up.

Art. 65 bis 5. If the necessities of a flagrante delicto investigation or of the preliminary inquiry relating to offences in the matter of drug trafficking, organized transnational crime, attacks on automated data processing systems, money laundering, terrorism and offences relating to exchange legislation as well as to corruption require it, the public prosecutor may authorize: the interception of correspondences emitted by way of telecommunications; the installation of a technical device whose object is, without the consent of the persons concerned, the capture, the fixation, the transmission and the recording of words pronounced by one or more persons in private or confidential settings in private or public places, or the image of one or more persons located in a private place. The authorization permits, for the installation of the technical device, the introduction into any place of dwelling or other, including outside the hours provided in Article 47 of this law, without the knowledge or without the consent of the persons having a right on these goods. Operations authorized thus must be carried out under the direct control of the competent public prosecutor.

Art. 65 bis 8. The public prosecutor or the judicial police officer authorized by him, the investigating judge or the judicial police officer appointed by him may require any agent qualified from a service, unit or public or private body in charge of telecommunications, in order to take charge of the technical aspects of the operations referred to in Article 65 bis 5."
