(Nicaragua 2020)_01,C_EXPRESS_NATSEC,False,,True,1.0,"Article 6 Interception of communications and transmissions between Information and Communication Technology systems
The person who illegitimately intercepts any type of written communication not addressed to them, or who using Information and Communication Technologies intercepts any transmission, to, from or within a computer system or any technological means that is not available to the public; or the electromagnetic emissions that are carrying data from a computer system, shall be punished with imprisonment of one to three years and two hundred to five hundred days-multas.

Article 21 Breach of confidentiality
Whoever breaches confidentiality about the information that they became aware of on the occasion of their participation in the process of investigation, collection, interception or intervention of data of a computer system or of its components, shall be imposed a penalty of one hundred to three hundred days-multas.

Article 22 Computer identity impersonation and appropriation
Whoever impersonates or takes over the computer identity of a natural or juridical person by means of Information and Communication Technologies, shall be imposed a penalty of three to five years of imprisonment and two hundred to five hundred days-multas.

Article 24 Use of personal data
Whoever without authorization uses personal data through the use of Information and Communication Technologies, violating systems of confidentiality and data security, inserting or modifying the data to the detriment of a third party, shall be imposed a penalty of four to six years of imprisonment and two hundred to five hundred days-multas.

Article 26 Improper revelation of personal data or information
If any of the conducts described in the preceding paragraph had been carried out with a view to profit, facilitates the commission of another crime or disseminates explicit sexual material to the detriment of a third party, the penalty shall be four to eight years of imprisonment and two hundred to five hundred days-multas.

Article 28 Threats through Information and Communication Technologies
Whoever threatens another through the use of Information and Communication Technologies with: 2. Making imputations against honor, or prestige, violating or disclosing secrets, to the detriment of them, their family, other persons with whom they are related, or an entity they represent or in which they have interest, shall be imposed a penalty of two to four years of imprisonment.

Article 28 Threats through Information and Communication Technologies
Whoever threatens another through the use of Information and Communication Technologies; if the threat is made in the name of real or supposed entities or groups, shall be imposed a penalty of three to five years of imprisonment.

Article 28 Threats through Information and Communication Technologies
Whoever threatens another through the use of Information and Communication Technologies; if the threat of a harm that constitutes a crime were directed to intimidate the inhabitants of a population, ethnic, cultural or religious group, social collective or any other group of people and had the necessary capacity to carry it out, shall be imposed a penalty of four to six years of imprisonment.

Article 30 Propagation of false news through Information and Communication Technologies
Whoever, using Information and Communication Technologies, publishes or disseminates false and/or distorted information that incites hatred and violence, endangers economic stability, public order, public health or sovereign security, shall be imposed a penalty of three to five years of imprisonment and five hundred to eight hundred days-multas.

Article 20 Violation of judicial custody of data
Whoever knowingly that a computer system or any of its components is under judicial custody and uses them, manipulates their records or contents, violates the seals or precints, shall be imposed a penalty of one to four years of imprisonment.

Article 20 Violation of judicial custody of data
If the action described in the preceding paragraph is carried out, facilitated or permitted by the person in charge of the judicial custody, they shall be imposed a penalty of two to five years of imprisonment.

Article 13 Computer espionage
Whoever improperly obtains sensitive personal data or reserved public information contained in a system that uses Information and Communication Technologies or in any of its components, shall be imposed a penalty of five to eight years of imprisonment and three hundred to six hundred days-multas."
