(Nicaragua 2020)_01,C_EXPRESS_OBSCENE,False,,True,1.0,"Article 22 Computer identity impersonation and appropriation
Whoever, with the conducts described in the preceding paragraph, harms, extorts, defrauds, injures or threatens another person in order to cause prejudice or obtain benefits for themselves or for third parties, shall be imposed a penalty of five to eight years of imprisonment and three hundred to six hundred days-multas.

Article 26 Improper revelation of personal data or information
The maximum limit of the penalty of the preceding paragraph shall be imposed, increased by up to one third, if any of the conducts described in this article fall upon sensitive personal data.

Article 28 Threats through Information and Communication Technologies
Whoever threatens another through the use of Information and Communication Technologies with: 1. Causing to them, to their family or to other persons with whom they are related, a harm that constitutes a crime and that by its nature seems plausible, shall be imposed a penalty of one to three years of imprisonment."
