(Nicaragua 2020)_01,C_EXPRESS_REPUTATION,False,,True,1.0,"Article 7 Illicit capture of others' communications through Information and Communication Technologies
Whoever illegitimately, making use of Information and Communication Technologies, or any other means, records or captures the words or conversations of others, whether these are video, images, codes, audio or text, not intended for the public, listens to or intervenes in private communications that are not addressed to them, shall be punished with imprisonment of one to three years and one hundred to three hundred days-multas.

Article 23 Unauthorized disclosure
Whoever without authorization makes known a code, password or any other means of access to a program, information or data stored in a device or technological equipment, with the purpose of profiting themselves, a third party or to commit a crime, shall be imposed a penalty of five to eight years of imprisonment and two hundred to five hundred days-multas.

Article 24 Use of personal data
The penalty shall increase by up to one third of the upper limit of the penalty provided in the preceding paragraph to whoever provides or reveals to another information recorded in a file or in a personal data bank whose secrecy they were obliged to preserve.

Article 25 Transfer of public reserved information
Whoever without authorization or exceeding that which had been granted to them, transfers Public information classified as reserved, in accordance with the law of the matter and which by using that information undermines a system or computer data or places in danger the sovereign security of the State, relying on any kind of Information and Communication Technologies, shall be imposed a penalty of five to eight years of imprisonment and two hundred to five hundred days-multas.

Article 26 Improper revelation of personal data or information
Whoever without the consent of the holder of the private and personal information, reveals, disseminates or cedes in whole or in part, such information or data, whether these are images, video, text, audio or others, obtained by means of Information and Communication Technologies, shall be imposed a penalty of three to six years of imprisonment and two hundred to five hundred days-multas.

Article 29 Provocation, apologia and inducement to the commission of crimes through Information and Communication Technologies
Whoever, making use of Information and Communication Technologies, incites, instigates, provokes or promotes the commission of crimes, extols the crime or exalts its author or participants or claims it for themselves, shall be imposed a penalty of three to five years of imprisonment and two hundred to five hundred days-multas.

Article 30 Propagation of false news through Information and Communication Technologies
Whoever, using Information and Communication Technologies, publishes or disseminates false and/or distorted information, that produces alarm, fear, unease in the population, or to a group or sector of it, to a person or to their family, shall be imposed the penalty of two to four years of imprisonment and three hundred to five hundred days-multas.

Article 30 Propagation of false news through Information and Communication Technologies
Whoever, using Information and Communication Technologies, publishes or disseminates false and/or distorted information that harms the honor, prestige or reputation of a person or their family, shall be imposed a penalty of one to three years of imprisonment and one hundred fifty to three hundred fifty days-multas.

Article 39 Request for judicial authorization
For that purpose, the Judge may carry out the intervention or interception of telecommunications in real time, according to the procedure established in Article 62 of Law No. 735, which shall be applicable to the offenses contained in this Law.

Article 16 Manipulation of records
Whoever abusing their functions of administration of technological platforms, public or private, disables, alters, hides, destroys, or makes unusable in whole or in part any information, data contained in an access or usage record of the components thereof, shall be imposed a penalty of five to eight years of imprisonment and three hundred to six hundred days-multas."
