(Nicaragua 2020)_01,GOV_REGULATOR,True,1.0,True,1.0,"Article 39 Request for judicial authorization
In the investigation stage for the obtaining and conservation of the information contained in computer systems or any of their components, judicial authorization by any District Criminal Judge shall be required, at a petition duly substantiated by the National Police or the Public Ministry. Once the process has been initiated, any of the parties may request authorization from the Judge of the case.

Article 37 Data preservation
The National Police or the Public Ministry, within the scope of their competence, shall act with the required celerity to preserve the data contained in a computer system or its components, or the system's traffic data, especially when these are vulnerable to loss or modification.

Article 41 Responsibility of the judicial custodian of computer systems
Whoever has been entrusted with the preservation of the computer system or any of its components, as well as of its content, shall preserve their confidentiality and integrity, preventing third parties, outside of the competent authorities, from having access to and knowledge of them.

Article 42 Confidentiality of the investigative process
Those who participate in the process of investigation, collection, interception, intervention of data of a computer system or of its components, shall keep confidential all the information that they become aware of about the execution of the acts performed by the competent authority."
(Nicaragua 2020)_01,GOV_REGULATOR_CRISIS,False,,False,,
(Nicaragua 2020)_01,GOV_WARRANT,True,1.0,True,1.0,"Article 39 Request for judicial authorization
For that purpose, the Judge may order a natural or juridical person the immediate delivery of the information that is found in a computer system or in any of its components.

Article 39 Request for judicial authorization
For that purpose, the Judge may order a natural or juridical person to preserve and maintain the integrity of a computer system or any of its components, to conserve traffic, connection, access or any other information that is in their possession or under their control and that may be useful to the investigation, for a period of up to ninety (90) days, this order being renewable once for the same term.

Article 39 Request for judicial authorization
For that purpose, the Judge may take into seizure or secure a computer system or any of its components, in whole or in part.

Article 39 Request for judicial authorization
For that purpose, the Judge may carry out and retain a copy of the content of the computer system or of any of its components.

Article 39 Request for judicial authorization
For that purpose, the Judge may make inaccessible or remove the content of a computer system or of any of its components that has been accessed for the investigation.

Article 39 Request for judicial authorization
For that purpose, the Judge may order the person who has knowledge about the operation of a computer system or of any of its components or about the data protection measures in said system, to provide the necessary information to carry out the corresponding investigations.

Article 39 Request for judicial authorization
For that purpose, the Judge may order the extraction, collection or recording of the data of a computer system or of any of its components, through the application of technological measures.

Article 39 Request for judicial authorization
For that purpose, the Judge may order the service provider to collect, extract or record the data relating to a user, as well as the data traffic in real time, through the application of technological measures.

Article 39 Request for judicial authorization
If the authorization is decreed after the Preliminary or Initial Hearing, as the case may be, the defense counsel shall be notified and shall have the right to be present in the performance of the act.

Article 41 Responsibility of the judicial custodian of computer systems
Whoever is in charge of custody shall not make use of the computer system or any of its components in custody for purposes other than those related to the investigative process."
