(Zimbabwe 2020)_01,GOV_REGULATOR,False,,True,-1.0,"Prohibition of gatherings
5. (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to any school, unless —
(a) a district health officer, in relation to any school within a district for which the district health officer is responsible, declares by any means likely to make such declaration known to the school or schools concerned, that any specified school or group or class of schools shall be regarded as a gathering for the purposes of this section.

Prohibition of gatherings
5. (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to any school, unless —
(b) a Director (Health Services), in relation to any local authority for which the Director (Health Services) is responsible, declares by any means likely to make such declaration known to the school or schools concerned, that any specified school or group or class of schools shall be regarded as a gathering for the purposes of this section.

Prohibition of gatherings
5. (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to any school, unless —
(c) the Minister, acting on the advice of the Chief Health Officer, declares by any means likely to make such declaration known to the school or schools concerned, that any specified school or group or class of schools shall be regarded as a gathering for the purposes of this section.

Prohibition of gatherings
5. (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to any school, unless —
(d) the Chief Health Officer, after consulting the Minister, declares by any means likely to make such declaration known to the school or schools concerned, that any specified school or group or class of schools shall be regarded as a gathering for the purposes of this section.

Ministerial orders
8. (1) In pursuance of the object of these regulations the Minister may (in consultation with the President, and in conformity with any directions the President may give) by orders published in the Gazette—
(b) close schools or regulate and restrict school attendance in any local authority;

Ministerial orders
8. (1) In pursuance of the object of these regulations the Minister may (in consultation with the President, and in conformity with any directions the President may give) by orders published in the Gazette—
(c) close places of worship and restrict gatherings or meetings forthe purpose of public worship in any local authority;"
