(El Salvador 1997)_02,C_EXPRESS_OBSCENE,False,,True,1.0,"Art. 18.- Operators of telecommunications services shall have the right to have aerial or underground lines in streets, plazas, parks, roads and other national public goods for the purposes of installing the networks necessary for the provision of services, subjecting themselves thereto to the norms applicable for that purpose.

Art. 31.- The suspension of the service does not invalidate the operators' right to resort to the pertinent judicial means.

Art. 122.- The operation of subscription television systems, by wired or wireless means, must not interfere in any way with the reception of open television signals that are broadcast in the same service area.

Art. 110.- Operators of access service that at the date of entry into force of this Law are operating, may not discontinue the services they were providing to the public in any population of the Republic, except as provided in Article 31.

Art. 35.- The General Superintendency of Electricity and Telecommunications may carry out technical consultations with international organizations recognized by means of treaties in force for that purpose."
