(El Salvador 1997)_02,C_EXPRESS_ORDER,False,,True,1.0,"Art. 15-A.- If no response is received from the Superintendence of Competition within the indicated period, it shall be understood as favorable and SIGET may continue with the respective procedure.

Art. 119-A.- The following are infractions of broadcasters: 2) Not providing information to SIGET when there is a legal obligation to do so, or providing false information.

Art. 119-A.- The infractions established above shall be sanctioned with a fine whose amount shall be between one thousand seven hundred United States Dollars and thirty-three thousand United States Dollars, in addition to a fine of fifty-seven point fourteen United States Dollars for each day that the infraction continues. The Regulation of this law shall determine the manner of application of this Article."
(El Salvador 1997)_02,I_EXPRESS_ORDER,False,,True,1.0,"Art. 19-A.- Fixed network telecommunications service providers are obliged to provide access to associated resources at reasonable and non-discriminatory prices, terms and conditions."
