(El Salvador 1997)_02,C_EXPRESS_RELIGION,False,,True,1.0,"Art. 2-A.- k) Technological Neutrality: freedom of network operators and providers of telecommunications services to choose and offer the technologies to be used, according to technological development, in a climate of free competition, complying with international standards that respond to the quality requirements and the needs of the user.

Art. 7.- Such concessions shall be granted without any limitation as to quantity and location, and more than one concession may exist in the same geographic area.

Art. 12.- For the exploitation of the official use spectrum, state institutions shall request the corresponding authorization.

Art. 12.- For the exploitation of the free use spectrum, no concession or authorization shall be required. However, SIGET shall qualify, for technical or planning reasons, those free use frequency bands that must have a license granted by it for their use.

Art. 14.- Operators of earth stations shall be responsible for the interference they cause in the operation of such stations.

Art. 15.- In any case, the holders of the exploitation right of the spectrum shall be responsible for violations arising from the use of the same.

Art. 20.- Each operator, at the time it requests access to an essential resource, shall have the right to enjoy contractual terms similar to those that the operator granting such resource has contracted with other operators.

Art. 20.- Access shall not be granted when the equipment to be interconnected may produce malfunction or damage to equipment in use.

Art. 20-A.- Fixed network operators that provide public telecommunications services shall not impose discriminatory or unreasonable prices, conditions or limitations for the resale of those services.

Art. 20-A.- Important fixed network providers may not offer such services on prices and conditions less favorable than those they supply to their own end users.

Art. 20-A.- Resellers shall register in advance in the Registry attached to SIGET.

Art. 26.- Pre-subscription shall not prevent the user from accessing the networks of intermediate services of other intermediate services operators that provide their services through the multi-carrier system.

Art. 115-A.- The concessionaires may transfer to any title or lease the right of exploitation of concessioned frequencies. Any sublease of frequencies shall be null."
