(El Salvador 1997)_02,C_EXPRESS_REPUTATION,False,,True,1.0,"Art. 29.- m) The operator is obliged to unlock the terminal equipment free of charge for the owner thereof once the service contract term for which the terminal was provided has expired. Under no circumstances may the blocking of the equipment exceed the contract term, which may not be greater than 18 months from its signature.

Art. 30.- b) Users must be answerable before the competent courts for the malfunction or damage they cause to the operators' network by connecting at the network termination points any equipment or device owned by them and obtained under any title.

Art. 31.- Operators may suspend the provision of their services without prior notice to the user only in the following cases: c) When connected to the telecommunications network without prior authorization of the access service operator.

Art. 115-A.- The concessionaires may transfer to any title or lease the right of exploitation of concessioned frequencies provided that the concessionaires comply with the following requirement 1: That the contract executed between the concessionaire and the acquirer or lessee be authorized by SIGET with respect to technical aspects.

Art. 115-A.- The concessionaires may transfer to any title or lease the right of exploitation of concessioned frequencies provided that the concessionaires comply with the following requirement 5: That the interested party and the applicant be solvent with respect to state tax obligations that are final and enforceable.

Art. 119-A.- The following are infractions of broadcasters: 1) Not registering in the Registry when there is a legal obligation to do so.

Art. 119-A.- The following are infractions of broadcasters: 4) Using the radio-electric spectrum without respecting the technical norms and conditions established in the CNAF.

Art. 120.- Natural or legal persons who apply to provide subscription broadcasting services, sound or television, must obtain beforehand an enabling title from SIGET and comply with the requirements established to that effect by SIGET and the respective Regulation. The foregoing is independent of the medium used, whether by radio-electric waves or by wired networks.

Art. 124.- The following are specific causes for the revocation of enabling titles: a) The lack of payment or incomplete payment of the annual fee established in Art. 116 of this Law, twenty days after the end of the term, after a hearing to the concessionaire; without contravening what is established in Art. 129 of this Law.

Art. 124.- The following are specific causes for the revocation of enabling titles: f) Failure to submit the annual declaration of the number of subscribers and channels that transmit or submitting it with false information.

Art. 127.- The President of the Republic shall have the right to convene all radio and television stations of the country for a national broadcast of radio and television for reasons of war, invasion of territory, rebellion, sedition, catastrophe, epidemic or other calamity, serious disturbances of public order or a message of national interest. The Supreme Electoral Tribunal may do so in the cases established in the Electoral Code. The concessionaires shall be obliged to transmit, at the requested time, the pilot signal of the Presidency of the Republic, without cuts or modifications of any kind. If for technical reasons any concessionaire is unable to transmit what is requested, it shall cease to broadcast its regular programming while the national broadcast lasts. Except in cases of force majeure or fortuitous event duly proven, the refusal of a concessionaire to transmit the national broadcast shall make it liable to a fine equivalent to the value of three times the annual fee for the first and second time; and six times for the third time or more.

Art. 98.- If the user does not receive any communication within the established period, the solution shall be considered in his favor, the operator being obliged to compensate him for the damages it has caused him. In case of undue charges, it shall refund the amount that the user has paid to the operator, without prejudice to the corresponding legal actions."
