(El Salvador 1997)_02,IM_PREVENTION,False,,True,1.0,"Art. 7.- In cases in which a concession for the provision of the public telephony service is revoked or extinguished, the SIGET shall inform in advance and with the necessary reasonable time the Ministry of Economy, in order to guarantee the continuity of the service.

Art. 31.- Operators may suspend the provision of their services without prior notice to the user only in the following cases: b) When malfunction or damage is caused to operators' networks by connection at the termination points of such network of any equipment or device owned by the user or obtained under any title.

Art. 31.- Operators may suspend the provision of their services without prior notice to the user only in the following cases: e) When ordered by judicial authority within the framework of a criminal procedure and investigation; a copy of such order shall be sent to SIGET.

Art. 85-H.- If the technical report is favorable the Superintendent shall issue a resolution granting the requested concession; the concession shall enter into force once payment has been made and in the case of authorizations they shall enter into force on the date of issuance of the resolution."
