(El Salvador 2024)_01,C_EXPRESS_ORDER,False,,True,1.0,"Art. 19.- Minor infractions. The holders, top management and any other official or employee shall also incur liability for the preceding infractions when these materialize by virtue of their order, instruction, negligence or omission.

Art. 20.- Serious infractions. The holders, top management and any other official or employee shall also incur liability for the preceding infractions when these materialize by virtue of their order, instruction, negligence or omission.

Art. 21.- Very serious infractions. The holders, top management and any other official or employee shall also incur liability for the preceding infractions when these materialize by virtue of their order, instruction, negligence or omission.

Art. 22.- Sanction for minor infractions. The subjects who commit minor infractions shall be sanctioned with a written reprimand or a fine of between one to ten monthly minimum wages of the commerce sector, as applicable to the obligated subject.
An official or employee who receives three or more written reprimands in a period of less than one year shall be dismissed from his employment or position without liability for the Public Administration.

Art. 26.- Additional measures. Once the sanction is determined to be appropriate, the Agency may order the infringer or the related obligated subject to adopt the measures necessary to restore the legality altered by the infraction or to correct the rights or situations violated.
All sanctions determined in this law do not exempt the infringer from civil or criminal liabilities arising from the corresponding investigations that they may give rise to.

Art. 29.- Prescription. The infractions and sanctions contemplated in this law shall prescribe after five years."
