(El Salvador 2024)_01,C_EXPRESS_PROPERTY,False,,True,1.0,"Art. 16.- Confidentiality. Authorities, officials, employees, delegates, experts, agents or persons who provide services to the Agency, in any capacity, whether temporary or permanent, are prohibited from revealing any information that they have obtained in the performance of their duties or from taking advantage of such information for personal or third-party purposes.

Art. 16.- Confidentiality. In the case of public servants who provide their services to the Agency, non-compliance with the provisions of this article shall constitute grounds for dismissal or removal from office without liability for the said authority, without prejudice to the civil, criminal or any other liability that may arise.

Art. 20.- Serious infractions. The subjects to whom this law applies shall be considered to commit the following serious infractions: f) Obstructing or preventing the tasks of the area or areas responsible for the implementation, monitoring, review and adaptation of actions and measures related to cybersecurity and information security.

Art. 21.- Very serious infractions. The subjects to whom this law applies shall be considered to commit the following very serious infractions: b) To present, without the required specifications, the reports or information related to cybersecurity and information security that are required by the competent authority, when such information is related to an incident or necessary for its management.

Art. 21.- Very serious infractions. The subjects to whom this law applies shall be considered to commit the following very serious infractions: g) Obstructing or preventing the management, audit and inspection tasks carried out by the Agency in cybersecurity and information security matters.

Art. 23.- Sanction for serious infractions. The subjects who commit serious infractions shall be sanctioned with dismissal or removal from office without liability for the Public Administration and a fine of between eleven to fifty monthly minimum wages of the commerce sector when the infringer is linked to the public sector.
If the infringer is from the private sector, the sanction shall be a fine of between eleven to fifty monthly minimum wages of the commerce sector.

Art. 24.- Sanction for very serious infractions. The subjects who commit very serious infractions shall be sanctioned with dismissal or removal from office without liability for the Public Administration and a fine of between fifty-one to one hundred monthly minimum wages of the commerce sector when the infringer is linked to the public sector.
If the infringer is from the private sector, the sanction shall be a fine of between fifty-one to one hundred monthly minimum wages of the commerce sector.

Art. 27.- Coercive fine. In order to achieve the execution of its acts, the Agency may impose coercive fines of between one to ten minimum wages of the commerce sector for each working day that transpires without compliance with what has been ordered.
This sanction shall be independent and compatible with the other sanctions contemplated in this law."
