(El Salvador 2024)_01,C_EXPRESS_REPUTATION,False,,True,1.0,"Art. 17.- Principles of legality, culpability and proportionality. The subjects obliged by this law shall be responsible for the administrative infractions established in this chapter, by action or omission, with intent, negligence or any other basis determined by the legal system.

Art. 19.- Minor infractions. The subjects to whom this law applies shall be considered to commit the following minor infractions: b) To present, without the required specifications, the reports or information related to cybersecurity and information security that are required by the Agency, provided that such information is not related to an incident or necessary for its management.

Art. 20.- Serious infractions. The subjects to whom this law applies shall be considered to commit the following serious infractions: g) Presenting incomplete, erroneous or inaccurate information to the Agency.

Art. 21.- Very serious infractions. The subjects to whom this law applies shall be considered to commit the following very serious infractions: i) Failing to comply with orders prohibiting the use of computer systems or any of their parts, in the time and manner communicated by the Agency."
