(Bolivia 2010)_01,C_EXPRESS_NATSEC,False,,True,1.0,"Article 1 69. ( FALSE T ESTIMONY). Anyone who, as a witness, expert, interpreter, translator or other person questioned in a judicial or administrative process, gives false testimony in a criminal trial to the detriment of the accused, shall incur deprivation of liberty from one (1) to three (3) years.

Article 1 69. ( FALSE T ESTIMONY). Anyone who commits false testimony through bribery shall have the preceding penalty increased by one third.

Article 1 66. ( FALSE A CCUSATION A ND DENUNCIATION). A nyone who k nowingly a ccuses o r r eports a s the a uthor o r p articipant o f a c rime o f p ublic action a p erson w ho d id n ot c ommit i t, g iving r ise to t he i nitiation o f the c orresponding c riminal process, will b e p unished with d eprivation of l iberty o f o ne ( 1) to t hree ( 3) years.

Article 281 Sexies.- (DISCRIMINATION). II. The penalty shall be increased by one third the minimum and by one half the maximum when: a) The act is committed by a public servant or public authority.

Article 281 Sexies.- (DISCRIMINATION). II. The penalty shall be increased by one third the minimum and by one half the maximum when: c) The act is committed with violence.

Article 363 B is. ( COMPUTER M ANIPULATION). Anyone who, with the intention of obtaining an undue benefit for himself or a third party, manipulates a processing or transfer of computer data that leads to an incorrect result or avoids such a process whose result would have been correct, thereby causing a transfer of assets to the detriment of a third party, shall be punished with imprisonment of one ( 1) to five (5) years and a fine of sixty ( 60) to two hundred (200) days."
