(Bolivia 2010)_01,C_EXPRESS_OBSCENE,False,,True,1.0,"Article 290. (RECIPROCAL OFFENSES). If the offenses or accusations are reciprocal, the judge may, depending on the circumstances, exempt both parties or one of them from punishment.

Article 300. (VIOLATION OF CORRESPONDENCE AND PRIVATE PAPERS). Anyone who improperly opens a letter, a sealed packet or a telegraphic, radiotelegraphic or telephone communication, addressed to another person, or who, without opening the correspondence, by technical means obtains information about its content, shall be punished with imprisonment from three (3) months to one (1) year or a fine of sixty (60) to two hundred and forty (240) days. The same penalty shall apply to anyone who similarly seizes, hides or destroys a letter, a packet, a dispatch or other private paper, even if it is open, or who arbitrarily diverts correspondence that does not belong to him from its destination. The maximum penalty will be raised to two (2) years, when the author of such acts discloses the content of the indicated correspondence and dispatches.

Article 301. (VIOLATION OF SECRETS IN CORRESPONDENCE NOT INTENDED FOR PUBLICITY). Anyone who records the words of another not intended for the public, without his consent, or who, through technical procedures, listens to private statements not addressed to him, or who does the same with private papers or with epistolary or telegraphic correspondence even if they were addressed to him, provided that the act may cause some harm, shall be punished with deprivation of liberty from three (3) months to one (1) year.

Article 281 Septies.- ( Dissemination and Incitement to Racism or Discrimination). Anyone who by any means disseminates ideas based on racial superiority or hatred, or that promote and/or justify racism or any form of discrimination, for the reasons described in articles 281 quinquies and 281 sexies, or incites violence or persecution of persons or groups of persons, based on racist or discriminatory motives, shall be punished with a prison sentence of one (1) to five (5) years.

Article 281 Septies.- ( Dissemination and Incitement to Racism or Discrimination). Anyone who by any means disseminates ideas based on racial superiority or hatred, or that promote and/or justify racism or any form of discrimination, for the reasons described in articles 281 quinquies and 281 sexies, or incites violence or persecution of persons or groups of persons, based on racist or discriminatory motives, shall be punished with a prison sentence of one (1) to five (5) years. The sanction will be increased by one third of the minimum and by one half of the maximum, when the act is committed by a public servant or authority.

Article 281 Sexies.- (DISCRIMINATION). I. Any person who arbitrarily and illegally obstructs, restricts, undermines, prevents or annuls the exercise of individual and collective rights, for reasons of sex, age, gender, sexual orientation and gender identity, cultural identity, family affiliation, nationality, citizenship, language, religious creed, ideology, political or philosophical opinion, marital status, economic or social condition, illness, type of occupation, degree of education, different abilities or physical, intellectual or sensory disability, pregnancy status, regional origin, physical appearance and clothing, shall be punished with a prison sentence of one (1) to five (5) years.

Article 281 Octies. (Racist or Discriminatory Organizations or Associations). Any person who participates in an organization or association that promotes and/or justifies racism or discrimination described in articles 281 quinquies and 281 sexies or incites hatred, violence or persecution of persons or groups of persons based on racist or discriminatory motives, shall be punished with imprisonment of one (1) to four (4) years. The penalty will be increased by one third the minimum and by one half the maximum, when the act is committed by a public servant or public authority.

Article 363 Ter. ( ALTERATION, ACCESS AND IMPROPER USE OF COMPUTER DATA). Whoever, without authorization, takes possession of, accesses, uses, modifies, deletes or renders useless data stored in a computer or any computer medium, causing harm to the owner of the information, will be sanctioned with work for up to one ( 1) year or a fine of up to two hundred (200) days."
