(Bolivia 2010)_01,C_EXPRESS_ORDER,False,,True,1.0,"Article 1 29. ( OUTRAGE TO N ATIONAL S YMBOLS). A nyone w ho publicly i nsults t he flag, the coat of a rms or the a nthem o f the N ation w ill b e punished w ith imprisonment of s ix (6) months t o t wo ( 2) years.

Article 1 30. ( PUBLIC I NSTIGATION T O C OMMIT C RIMES). A nyone who publicly i nstigates t he commission of a s pecific c rime shall be punished with i mprisonment of o ne ( 1) month t o o ne (1) year.

Article 1 30. ( PUBLIC I NSTIGATION T O C OMMIT C RIMES). Anyone who publicly instigates the commission of a specific crime, if the instigation refers to a crime against state security, public service or the national economy, shall be punished with imprisonment from three (3) months to two (2) years.

Article 1 31. ( PUBLIC A POLOGY O F A C RIME). A nyone who publicly p raises a crime o r a convicted p erson will b e subject t o imprisonment f rom o ne ( 1) month t o o ne (1) year.

Article 1 62. ( CONTEMPT). A nyone who by any m eans s landers, i nsults o r d efames a p ublic o fficial i n t he exercise o f his o r h er f unctions or b ecause o f t hem, s hall b e p unished with d eprivation of l iberty f rom o ne ( 1) month to two (2) y ears.

Article 1 62. ( CONTEMPT). Anyone who by any means slanders, insults or defames a public official in the exercise of his or her functions or because of them, if such acts are directed against the President or Vice President of the Republic, Ministers of State or the Supreme Court or a member of Congress, shall incur a sanction increased by one half.

Article 1 11. (ESPIONAGE) Anyone w ho p rocures secret d ocuments, objects or information of a p olitical or m ilitary nature relating t o security, m eans of d efense or foreign r elations, for the purposes of e spionage in favor o f o ther c ountries i n times o f peace, which endanger t he s ecurity of t he S tate, shall i ncur a p enalty of thirty (30) years of imprisonment w ithout t he r ight to p ardon.

Article 1 12. (CLANDESTINE I NTRODUCTION A ND P OSSESSION O F E SPIONAGE MEANS). A nyone who, in t ime o f war, c landestinely, d eceitfully o r violently e nters a m ilitary place o r zone o r is c aught i n s uch places or in t heir v icinity in unjustified possession o f e spionage means, w ill incur a p rison sentence o f f ive (5) t o t en (10) years.

Article 1 15. ( REVELATION O F S ECRETS). Anyone who reveals secrets of a political or military nature concerning the security of the State, the means of defense or foreign relations, if the agent commits this crime by abusing the function, employment or commission conferred by public authority, shall incur an increased penalty by one third.

Article 1 16. ( CRIME B Y F AULT). If t he revelation of t he s ecrets m entioned in the p revious a rticle i s committed through t he fault of t he person w ho is i n p ossession, b y v irtue o f h is e mployment o r o ffice, t he sanction will be imprisonment f rom s ix (6) months t o t wo ( 2) years.

Article 1 70. ( BRIBERY). W hoever o ffers or p romises m oney or any appreciable a dvantage to t he p ersons r eferred to i n t he p revious article, in order to o btain f alse t estimony, e ven if t he offer or promise h as not b een accepted or if it has been, t he f alsehood w as n ot b een committed, s hall i ncur imprisonment o f o ne (1) to t wo ( 2) y ears and a fine of t hirty ( 30) t o o ne hundred (100) days.

Article 1 67. ( SIMULATION OF C RIME). A nyone who k nowingly r eports o r m akes a n a uthority believe t hat a non-existent public action crime h as been committed, w hich g ives r ise to t he i nstruction o f a p rocess t o v erify it, will be p unished with w ork performance f rom t hree ( 3) months t o o ne ( 1) y ear.

Article 1 68. (SELF-CALUMNY). Anyone who commits self-calumny, if the act is committed in the interest of a close relative or a person of close friendship, may be exempt from punishment.

Article 1 141. (OUTRAGE TO T HE FLAG, THE C OAT O F A RMS OR THE ANTHEM O F A F OREIGN STATE). Anyone w ho p ublicly i nsults the flag, t he c oat of a rms o r the a nthem o f a f oreign n ation s hall be punished w ith i mprisonment f rom t hree (3) months t o o ne (1) y ear.

Article 226. (AGIO). Anyone who attempts to raise or lower the price of goods, wages or negotiable securities in the market or stock exchange, through false news, fake negotiations or any other fraudulent artifice, will incur a prison sentence of six (6) months to three (3) years, aggravated by one third if any of these effects occur.

Article 237. (DISTRIBUTION OF CUSTOMER TIME). Anyone who, using false statements, suspicions, fraudulent tricks or any other means of unfair advertising, diverts the clientele of a commercial or industrial establishment for his own benefit or that of a third party and to the detriment of the competitor, in order to obtain an undue advantage, shall incur a fine of thirty (30) to one hundred (100) days.

Article 282. (DEFAMATION). Anyone who publicly, tendentiously and repeatedly reveals or divulges a fact, quality or conduct capable of affecting the reputation of an individual or collective person, will incur a work permit of one (1) month to one (1) year or a fine of twenty (20) to two hundred and forty (240) days.

Article 284. (OFFENSE TO THE MEMORY OF THE DECEASED). Anyone who offends the memory of a deceased person with defamatory expressions or slanderous accusations shall incur the same penalties as in the two previous articles.

Article 285. (SPREADING OF OFFENSES). Anyone who spreads or reproduces by any means the facts referred to in Articles 282, 283 and 284 shall be punished as the author thereof.

Article 286. (EXCEPTION OF TRUTH). The author of defamation and slander shall not be punishable if the accusations consist of true statements, but the accused may only prove the truth of the accusation: 1) When the offenses are directed at a public official and in reference to his or her functions. 2) When the complainant requests proof of the charge, provided that such proof does not affect the rights or secrets of a third party.

Article 286. (EXCEPTION OF TRUTH). The author of defamation and slander shall not be punishable if the accusations consist of true statements, but the accused may only prove the truth of the accusation: 1) When the offenses are directed at a public official and in reference to his or her functions.

Article 287. (INFRINGEMENT). Anyone who by any means and in a direct manner offends another person in his dignity or decorum, will incur a work permit of one (1) month to one (1) year and a fine of thirty (30) to one hundred (100) days. If the act provided for in article 283 and the insult referred to in this article were committed by means of printed, typewritten or handwritten material, its author will be considered guilty of defamatory libel and punished with a fine of sixty (60) to one hundred and fifty (150) days, without prejudice to the corresponding penalties.

Article 288. (INTERDICTION OF EVIDENCE). Evidence will not be admitted except in cases indicated in article 286.

Article 289. (RETRACTION). The person accused of a crime against honor shall be exempt from punishment if he retracts his statement before or in time of giving his testimony. A second retraction regarding the same fact will not be permitted.

Article 281 Sexies.- (DISCRIMINATION). II. The penalty shall be increased by one third the minimum and by one half the maximum when: b) The act is committed by a private individual in the provision of a public service.

Article 281 Quinquies.- ( RACISM). II. The penalty shall be increased by one third the minimum and by one half the maximum when: a) The act is committed by a public servant or public authority.

Article 281 Quinquies.- ( RACISM). II. The penalty shall be increased by one third the minimum and by one half the maximum when: b) The act is committed by a private individual in the provision of a public service.

Article 281 Quinquies.- ( RACISM). II. The penalty shall be increased by one third the minimum and by one half the maximum when: c) The act is committed with violence.

Article 71. ( Illegality of evidence). Prosecutors may n ot use against t he accused e vidence o btained in v iolation o f the Political Constitution of the State, international c onventions a nd treaties in f orce and the laws.

Article 111. ( Language). Spanish shall be the language used in all procedural acts, without prejudice to statements or interrogations being made in the language of the declarant. To verify that the record is true, the declarant will have the right to request the intervention of one ( 1) translator of his or her choice, who will sign the document as a sign of conformity.

Article 93. ( Prohibited methods for making a statement). I n n o c ase shall t he accused be required to s wear a n oath, n or shall h e be s ubjected to a ny kind of c oercion, threat or promise, n or shall any means be used to f orce, induce or instigate him t o m ake a statement against his will; n or shall charges b e brought against him in o rder to o btain h is c onfession. The statement of t he accused without t he presence of the prosecutor and his defense attorney that contains a confession of the crime will be void and may not be used in the process, without prejudice to the administrative responsibility of those who receive or use it. If, due to the duration of the hearing, signs of fatigue or lack of composure are noted in the accused, the statement will be suspended until these signs disappear. In all cases, the statement of the accused will be made in a suitable place.

Article 283. (Controlled delivery). The decision of the investigating judge authorizing controlled delivery shall be kept confidential and kept outside the proceedings with due security, in a sealed envelope."
