(Bolivia 2010)_01,C_EXPRESS_REPUTATION,False,,True,1.0,"Article 1 66. ( FALSE A CCUSATION A ND DENUNCIATION). Anyone who knowingly accuses or reports as the author or participant of a crime of public action a person who did not commit it, if as a consequence the conviction of the accused or reported person occurs, shall be punished with deprivation of liberty from two (2) to six (6) years.

Article 283. (SLANDER). Anyone who by any means falsely accuses another of committing a crime shall be punished with imprisonment from six (6) months to three (3) years and a fine of one hundred (100) to three hundred (300) days.

Article 286. (EXCEPTION OF TRUTH). The author of defamation and slander shall not be punishable if the accusations consist of true statements, but the accused may only prove the truth of the accusation: 2) When the complainant requests proof of the charge, provided that such proof does not affect the rights or secrets of a third party.

Article 296. (CRIMES AGAINST FREEDOM OF THE PRESS). Anyone who illegally commits a crime shall be punished with imprisonment from six (6) months to three (3) years and a fine of thirty (30) to two hundred (200) days. prevents or hinders the free expression of thought through any means of dissemination, as well as the free circulation of a book, newspaper or any other printed matter.

Article 302. (REVELATION OF PROFESSIONAL SECRETS). Anyone who, having knowledge of secrets by virtue of his status, ministry, profession, employment, trade, art or commission, reveals them without just cause, or uses them for his own benefit or that of another, if any harm should result from this, shall be punished with imprisonment from three (3) months to one (1) year and a fine of thirty (30) to one hundred (100) days.

Article 281 Septies.- ( Dissemination and Incitement to Racism or Discrimination). Anyone who by any means disseminates ideas based on racial superiority or hatred, or that promote and/or justify racism or any form of discrimination, for the reasons described in articles 281 quinquies and 281 sexies, or incites violence or persecution of persons or groups of persons, based on racist or discriminatory motives, shall be punished with a prison sentence of one (1) to five (5) years. The sanction will be increased by one third of the minimum and by one half of the maximum, when the act is committed by a worker of a means of employment, social communication, or owner thereof, immunity or any jurisdiction may not be claimed.

Article 281 Quinquies.- ( RACISM). I. The person who arbitrarily and illegally restricts, annuls, undermines or prevents the exercise of individual or collective rights for reasons of race, national or ethnic origin, color, ancestry, belonging to indigenous nations and peoples peasants or the Afro-Bolivian people or the use of their own clothing or language, will be punished with a prison sentence of three (3) to seven (7) years.

Article 281 Octies. (Racist or Discriminatory Organizations or Associations). Any person who participates in an organization or association that promotes and/or justifies racism or discrimination described in articles 281 quinquies and 281 sexies or incites hatred, violence or persecution of persons or groups of persons based on racist or discriminatory motives, shall be punished with imprisonment of one (1) to four (4) years.

Article 281 Nonies. (Insults and other verbal aggressions for racist or discriminatory reasons). Anyone who by any means makes insults or other verbal aggressions, for racist or discriminatory motives described in articles 281 quinquies and 281 sexies, will incur a work permit of forty days to eighteen (18) months and a fine of forty (40) to one hundred and fifty (150) days.

Article 281 Nonies. (Insults and other verbal aggressions for racist or discriminatory reasons). Anyone who by any means makes insults or other verbal aggressions, for racist or discriminatory motives described in articles 281 quinquies and 281 sexies, will incur a work permit of forty days to eighteen (18) months and a fine of forty (40) to one hundred and fifty (150) days. YO. If this crime were committed by means of printed, handwritten or through means of communication, the penalty will be increased by one third the minimum and by one half the maximum.

Article 281 Nonies. (Insults and other verbal aggressions for racist or discriminatory reasons). Anyone who by any means makes insults or other verbal aggressions, for racist or discriminatory motives described in articles 281 quinquies and 281 sexies, will incur a work permit of forty days to eighteen (18) months and a fine of forty (40) to one hundred and fifty (150) days. II. If the person accused of this crime retracts, before or at the time of the formal charge, The criminal action shall be extinguished. A second retraction on the same fact shall not be permitted.

Article 281 Nonies. (Insults and other verbal aggressions for racist or discriminatory reasons). Anyone who by any means makes insults or other verbal aggressions, for racist or discriminatory motives described in articles 281 quinquies and 281 sexies, will incur a work permit of forty days to eighteen (18) months and a fine of forty (40) to one hundred and fifty (150) days. III. The retraction must be made by the same means, under the same conditions and scope as the in which the insult or verbal aggression took place, assuming the costs that this entails.

Article 113. ( Hearings). Spanish shall be the language used in the trial and in other oral hearings. Alternatively, by means of a reasoned resolution, the judge or court may order the use of the native language of the place where the trial is held. If any of the parties, judges or declarants do not easily understand the language or tongue used, the judge or court shall appoint a common translator.

Article 116. (Publicity). Within the framework of the responsibilities established by the Press Law, journalistic information on a criminal process will refrain from presenting the accused as guilty, as long as he has not been convicted.

Article 116. (Publicity). The investigating judge or the sentencing judge or court may order, by means of a reasoned resolution, that certain acts of the proceedings be carried out confidentially, in whole or in part, when: 2) The physical integrity of the judges, of any of the parties, or of any person is at risk cited.

Article 116. (Publicity). The investigating judge or the sentencing judge or court may order, by means of a reasoned resolution, that certain acts of the proceedings be carried out confidentially, in whole or in part, when: 4) He the accused or the victim is under eighteen (18) years of age.

Article 362. (CRIMES A GAINST INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY). W hoever, for profit, t o t he d etriment o f another, reproduces, plagiarizes, distributes, publishes on screen or on television, in whole or in part, a literary, artistic, musical, scientific, television or cinematographic work, or its transformation, interpretation, artistic performance through any means, without the authorization of the owners of the intellectual property rights or their concessionaires, or imports, exports or stores copies of said works, without the aforementioned authorization, shall be punished with imprisonment from three (3) months to two (2) years and a fine of sixty (60) days."
