(Bolivia 2010)_01,IM_PREVENTION,True,1.0,True,1.0,"Article 94. ( Defense attorney). The accused's statements may not be made without the presence of his defense attorney. In the event of non-attendance, a new hearing will be set for the following day, and he will be formally summoned; if he does not appear, another attorney will be immediately appointed, without prejudice to any corresponding sanctions. When it is impossible for the accused to receive technical assistance at the hearing, due to the absence of a lawyer at the location or the failure of those designated for this purpose to appear, he may be assisted by a person with legal knowledge. Failure to comply with this rule will not allow the information obtained to be used against the declarant."
