(Angola 2020)_01,C_EXPRESS_NATSEC,False,,True,1.0,"ARTICLE 2 93
(Public incitement to crime)
2. If t he conduct described i n the p revious n umber results the c ommission o f t he crime, the a gent i s punished a s the i nstigator of the crime committed.

ARTICLE 3 17
(Espionage)
3. If t he a gent c ommits one of the a cts described i n the previous numbers, the perpetrator shall be punished with a prison sentence of 10 to 12 years in the case of paragraph 1 and 12 to 15 years in the case of paragraph 2.

ARTICLE 319
(Collection o f military information)
1. An organization whose purpose is to gather military information, recruit informants or support any of these activities is punishable by imprisonment of 3 to 8 years.

ARTICLE 319
(Collection o f military information)
2. If the offender commits the act referred to in the previous number in the service of a prohibited or illegal association or organization, or of foreign entities or services, to undermine the military capacity of the Angolan Armed Forces or endanger it, the penalty is imprisonment of 8 to 12 years.

ARTICLE 3 77
(Incitement to hatred against a people and advocacy of w ar)
1. W hoever repeatedly and publicly incites hatred a gainst a people, w ith the p urpose o f s tarting a war, i s punished with a prison sentence of 1 to 8 years.

ARTICLE 4 38
(Illegitimate a ccess t o i nformation system and b reach through i nformation s ystem)
1. Anyone who, without authorization, accesses all or part of an information system of which they are not the owner, shall be punished with a prison sentence of up to 2 years or a fine of up to 240 days.

ARTICLE 4 38
(Illegitimate a ccess t o i nformation system and b reach through i nformation s ystem)
2. Anyone who gains access by violating security rules or who gains access through a protected service shall be punished with imprisonment of 2 to 8 years.

ARTICLE 4 38
(Illegitimate a ccess t o i nformation system and b reach through i nformation s ystem)
3.a) Anyone who, in the case described in paragraph 1, becomes aware of a trade secret shall be punished with the same penalty.

