(Angola 2020)_01,GOV_REGULATOR,False,,True,1.0,"ARTICLE 93
(Advertising o f the c onviction) 1. Whenever n ecessary for t he useful effect o f t he p enalty granted, applied, f or the reparation of the damage c aused b y the c rime, f or the p rotection of the assets a nd interests affected b y t he v iolated norm, a nd In general, f or the p urposes o f preventing a nd s uppressing crime, the C ourt o rders the p ublication o f the c onviction.
2. The p ublicity of the c onviction d ecision i s carried out a t the expense o f the c onvicted p erson, in a media outlet minimum l imit of 10 d ays a nd maximum of 3 60. resorting to means or mechanisms best s uited to safeguarding the effects underlying t he c onviction.
3. T he C ourt m ay order the p ublication o f the c onviction d ecision b y
4. T he p ublication o f the c onviction d ecision i s m ade by extract, which contains the e lements of the o ffence and t he consequences o f the act and its burden on w orkers collective o r similar entities.

ARTICLE 1 58
(Circulation o f m eans for t ermination o f p regnancy)
Anyone w ho receives o r t ransmits, by any m eans, m eans intended for the termination of pregnancy, with the intention of
promoting t he p ractice of t he a cts provided f or in a rticles 1 54 a nd 1 55, shall b e punished w ith a p rison s entence o f u p to 1
year o r a f ine o f u p t o 1 20 d ays.

ARTICLE 3 56
(Violation o f judicial s ecrecy)
Anyone w ho d iscloses acts, f acts o r t he content o f documents i n a case p rotected b y judicial secrecy o r t o which the Procedural L aw or t he judge d oes n ot allow public a ccess shall b e punished with a prison sentence of up to 3 years or a fine of up to 360 days."
